OL,3,GNEWSAWhy face coverings could be banned
OL,4,Ain Redditch
OL,5,
OL,6,FUnder the current legislation,
OL,7,Fofficials can only ask people to remove
OL,8,Fcoverings if they "reasonably believe"
OL,9,Fthey are being used to conceal their
OL,10,Fidentity, to commit crime or
OL,11,Fanti-social behaviour.
OL,13,F"I've seen it myself," Piolo said.
OL,14,F"Some of these young people are on
OL,15,Fmopeds with their faces covered up
OL,16,Fcausing mayhem."
